{
  "format": "avgen-project",
  "version": 4,
  "_note": "The permanent visual fixture for the shot-level camera presets. Six shots, six seconds each, one per behaviour, in the order the handbook explains them -- so `--render` produces a single clip in which the differences are side by side in time. Render it and the distinctions are not arguable: shot 1 the camera does not move, shot 2 it travels with the performer, shot 3 the performer stands still and the camera circles, shot 4 the camera IS the performer.",
